Requirements:
    Node.js 22.12 or newer (Node 24 LTS recommended; see .nvmrc).
    Tested with Node 24.18.1 and npm 12.2.0.
    Use the npm that ships with Node. Do not use yarn or pnpm: package-lock.json is the
    source of truth for dependency versions.

Pinned dependencies (exact versions come from package-lock.json):
    three           0.169.0
    three-mesh-bvh  0.8.3    (bundled into the build by Vite; imported from src/main.js)
    vite            5.4.21   (dev dependency)

Install dependencies (clean, reproducible install from package-lock.json):
    npm ci

Run the game locally (Vite dev server, http://localhost:5173):
    npm run dev

Windows PowerShell:
    If npm reports that npm.ps1 cannot run because scripts are disabled, use
    npm.cmd instead of npm for the commands in this README (for example,
    npm.cmd ci and npm.cmd run dev).

Build for deployment (output goes to dist/, which uses relative paths so it can be
hosted in a subdirectory):
    npm run build

Check the built game locally:
    npm run preview

Run the dialogue, collision, and Level 2 picture collection/scoring checks:
    npm test

Run only the Level 2 regression checks (no browser or model assets needed):
    node --test _verify_level2.mjs

Push your branch:
    Check "git status" and commit the files you intend to publish first.
    For the first push of the current branch, run:
    git push --set-upstream origin HEAD
    Subsequent pushes can use "git push".

Changing dependencies:
    Only use "npm install <package>" when you intend to add or change a dependency, then
    commit package.json and package-lock.json together. "npm ci" fails if they disagree.
    npm 12 blocks dependency install scripts unless they are listed under "allowScripts"
    in package.json. After changing dependencies, run "npm install-scripts ls" and keep the
    list matching the locked versions.

Project tracker: https://tadccgv.atlassian.net/jira/software/projects/KAN/summary
